    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0719" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg699"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 1, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to bring under your notice
                    the enclosed copy of a letter from a Mr. A. N. Thompson, which has been
                    forwarded to me by her Majesty’s consul at New York, relative to the liability
                    of British subjects to military service, from the mere fact of their having
                    voted at <hi rendition="#italic">school meetings.</hi></p>
                <p>I should be glad to be informed, at your earliest convenience, whether a State
                    election and a school meeting are to be considered to be on the same footing as
                    regards citizenship.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d478-a1.xml" xpointer="d478-a1"/>
            </div>
